# A MIDI Start with SID+CLK: the clock coming in starts on its beat 1, and the tune, which cannot start
# earlier, starts at its own first beat (run ahead silently to it, every write still reaching the
# chip), so the two are together from the first beat with no catching up. Commando's clock moved
# 100 ms later (KNOB 3) stands in for a tune whose first beat comes after its start
sid @SID1@
turn K2 3
wait 500
tap PLAY
wait 4000
tap GLO
turn K3 20
wait 200
expect clk_offset 100
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect playing 0
clockin 120 1
wait 2000
midi fa 0 0
wait 300
expect playing 1
expect follow 1
expect follow_err <200
expect follow_speed >3880
expect follow_speed <3970
wait 3000
expect follow_err <40
